<title>USA: Glendale, Coast up on court action.</title>
<headline>Glendale, Coast up on court action.</headline>
<dateline>GLENDALE, Calif 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Glendale Federal Bank, Coast Savings Financial Inc and other thrifts rose after scoring a victory in a longstanding goodwill lawsuit against the federal government.</p>
<p>Glendale and other thrifts are seeking billions of dollars in combined damages from the federal government for breach of contract in the 1980s. Last summer, a U.S. Supreme Court ruled the federal government was liable for damages.</p>
<p>The U.S. Court of Federal Claims Wednesday denied a government motion, ruling Glendale may present evidence in support of alternative measures of damages and restitution.</p>
</text>
